  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe shallow surface boundary will stall somewhere across northern \nMissouri on Tuesday and favor the more northern solutions for this \nboundary location given the west/southwest flow aloft and how \nshallow the feature is. Moisture will overrun this boundary and will \nbring increasing chances for showers and storms to parts of central \nand southern Iowa. MUCAPE values may approach 1000 J/kg over far \nsouthern Iowa. This does look possible and should saturation occur \nnear 800-850 mb, lapse rate above this level are sufficient for\nthis MUCAPEs and could support marginally large hail. The \ngreater chance for showers and storms arrive Wednesday night \ninto Thursday as the main upper low lifts northeast into the \nregion. A strong system diving south out of Canada will quickly \npush the precipitation out of the area. Much cooler temperatures\nwill follow with highs in the 50s and 60s and overnight lows in\nthe 30s along with the potential for frost perhaps as early as \nFriday night.",
